# A service account key grants full read and write over the entire Firebase
# project, bypassing every security rule. One must never reach the
# repository, so every .json here is ignored by default and the handful that
# belong in git are allowed back by name. Adding a file means allowing it
# deliberately, which is the right way round for a directory that is
# expected to contain a credential.
*.json
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json

node_modules/
# Generated reports contain real student data.
out/
